# herdr third-party plugin manifest
# Format: <owner>/<repo>[/<subdir>]@<git-ref>
# Blank lines and # comments are ignored by install.sh.
#
# The ref is required and pinned to a commit SHA. `herdr plugin install`
# without --ref resolves whatever HEAD happens to be, so two machines set up a
# week apart end up on different plugin code with nothing in the repo recording
# the difference. Bump a pin deliberately; re-running install.sh replaces the
# managed checkout.
#
# Locally-authored plugins do NOT belong here — they live in
# personal/herdr/plugins/ and are wired with `herdr plugin link`.

# Apply tab/pane layout templates on worktree.created / worktree.opened.
# Templates come from ~/.config/herdr/layouts.toml (see personal/herdr/README.md).
shopify-playground/herdr-plugins/worktree-layouts@04e318414ab58e2296b54c69e615b68496f750c3

# Move the active tab, panes and split layout intact, to another workspace.
# Bound to prefix+m / ctrl+alt+m in config.toml. Authored here, upstreamed in
# shopify-playground/herdr-plugins#7 — so it is pinned rather than linked.
shopify-playground/herdr-plugins/tab-mover@c8ff889f6e6a568cbcf0a6a1e3eeb8e8ddd76689

# One fzf modal over every keybinding, running agent, workspace, and file.
# Bound to prefix+space in config.toml. Authored here, upstreamed in
# shopify-playground/herdr-plugins#8 — so it is pinned rather than linked.
shopify-playground/herdr-plugins/launcher@9566d817294aae25804505ee827c0956580afbee

# Deliberately NOT the sibling `world` plugin: its picker enumerates
# `dev tree list`, which includes every WTP pool slot, and its rm action runs
# `dev tree remove`. `wtp free` only detaches HEAD, so one wrong pick destroys a
# slot that WTP itself would have preserved.
# shopify-playground/herdr-plugins/world@<sha>
